        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>I believe the answer to this is yes. If I remember correctly, MigrantP has stated that the game tracks the unlocks of Variants with two variables. If you unlock it with a code, itll fill in the variable that tells the game you used a code. If you unlock it legitimately, it fills in the variable that says you did the challenge. When the achievements are added, they&#39;ll look at the variable related to the challenges for confirmation of completion, which if you already did it should just auto-complete any achievements when you open up the game.</p>",
